# A SQL query too complex to rewrite: one DS0105 with a general example.
mode: syntax
---- query
SELECT customerId, count(*)
FROM orders
GROUP BY customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..60
  PIPELINE@0..59
    ERROR@0..59
      IDENT@0..6 "SELECT"
      WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
      IDENT@7..17 "customerId"
      COMMA@17..18 ","
      WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
      IDENT@19..24 "count"
      L_PAREN@24..25 "("
      STAR@25..26 "*"
      R_PAREN@26..27 ")"
      WHITESPACE@27..28 "\n"
      IDENT@28..32 "FROM"
      WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
      IDENT@33..39 "orders"
      WHITESPACE@39..40 "\n"
      IDENT@40..45 "GROUP"
      WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
      IDENT@46..48 "BY"
      WHITESPACE@48..49 " "
      IDENT@49..59 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@59..60 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `SELECT ... FROM` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:1
  |
1 | SELECT customerId, count(*)
  | ^^^^^^ this is SQL
2 | FROM orders
  | ---- in DataScript the table comes first
  |
  = help: start with the table and pipe it into operators: `'orders.csv' | where amount > 10 | project customerId, amount`
